  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. by Newton&#39;s law&nbsp;of cooling <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. According to Stephan&#39;s&nbsp;law&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#963;</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>283</mn><mn>293</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is correct</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The efficiency of the Carnot cycle is given by<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>.&nbsp;is wrong as according to the Newton&#39;s law of cooling&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
